   "chapeau": "Just how closely does GTA 6 resemble its real-world inspiration? Judging by a recent image comparison, the resemblance is striking. Many fans apparently couldn't tell the screenshot and the real photo apart at first glance.",
   "txt": "Reddit user u/Alex200496 has compared a screenshot from GTA 6 with a real photograph taken in Miami . The photo was reportedly taken at Joia Beach on Watson Island, located in Biscayne Bay between Downtown Miami and Miami Beach. Although the two images don't line up perfectly, contrary to what the Reddit post suggests, they still make for an interesting comparison.\nⓘ u/Alex200496 Which image shows the real Miami, and which is the screenshot? Many fans weren't sure at first glance. The real photo is, of course, the bottom image. For fans who have already seen the screenshot countless times, the difference was easy to spot. However, many Reddit users also admitted that they couldn't distinguish the real photo from the GTA 6 screenshot at first glance. A closer look, though, reveals several clues that give the game away.\nThe most obvious clue is the water. While Rockstar has done an impressive job rendering it, the surface still looks a little too uniform compared to real water. The noticeably sparser vegetation in the screenshot is another giveaway. Anyone familiar with Miami's skyline should also be able to spot the difference fairly quickly. Reddit users point out that the One Thousand Museum and 900 Biscayne skyscrapers are missing.\nAlthough Vice City isn't an exact replica of Miami, its graphics appear convincing enough to fool some viewers at first glance. Whether GTA 6 ( available for pre-order on Amazon ) will impress everyone visually remains to be seen, especially in light of a recent community discussion . Did you recognize the screenshot right away? Let us know in the comments below.",
