   "chapeau": "Learn how to play GTA 6 early on PS5 using the New Zealand trick with this super handy, short-form guide, complete with time zone breakdown.",
   "txt": "Grand Theft Auto 6 is arguably the most important game ever made . It’s the culmination of a decade of work and waiting, and it’s almost here . It’s anticipated to sell tens of millions of copies within a single week, and it’ll likely shatter records from the minute it hits the market.\nIf you want to be among the first to play Grand Theft Auto 6 early on PlayStation 5, you’ll want to know how to do the ‘New Zealand trick’, which effectively gets you the earliest access possible. To learn how to do the New Zealand trick on PS5, simply read on, as I’ve got the simplest guide for you, with all steps included.\nGrand Theft Auto 6 is coming out on November 19, unlocking at midnight local time around the world. That means that some territories will be able to access the game ‘earlier’ than others, thanks to how time zones work.\nNew Zealand is always the first territory to access new games because of where it’s situated on the planet. Isn’t that lovely for them?\nBut you can use a (relatively) easy trick to play GTA 6 early on PS5, using this New Zealand method to unlock the game 12 or 13 hours earlier than you normally would.\nThe problem is, PlayStation presents a rather troublesome approach to the trick , as you need to jump through some hoops to get GTA 6 early on PS5. It’s not as easy as it is to do the New Zealand trick on XBOX , where you just need to flip a switch in the console’s settings menu.\nHere are the steps to follow to unlock GTA 6 early on PlayStation 5:\nThere’s an additional step to consider if you want to play GTA 6 on your own account as opposed to the New Zealand account.\nWhen you come to the second step after making a New Zealand-based PSN account, you’ll want to head to your console settings, then to Users and Accounts, then Other, then Console Sharing and Offline Play, and flick that over to ‘enable’.\nWhen GTA comes out, you’ll be able to jump back to your main PlayStation 5 profile, and because you’ve enabled local sharing, you’ll be able to access the game early via your own account. It’s an extra step but it’s worthwhile doing.\nHere’s a handy table to help you understand when you can play GTA 6 using the New Zealand trick:\nAre you going to be using the New Zealand trick to play GTA 6 earlier? Let us know your plans on the Insider Gaming Discord server .\nFor more Insider Gaming coverage, check out whether it’s better to buy the Ultimate Edition of GTA 6 . And for even more Insider Gaming delivered directly to your inbox, sign up for our newsletter\nGrant has been gaming for 30+ years and in the industry for 10+. You'll probably find him playing a post-apocalyptic game or an extraction shooter somewhere.",
