   "chapeau": "Rockstar Games has confirmed that GTA 6 preloading begins on November 10, 2026, with a download size of up to 212 GB. The game will launch on November 19 at midnight local time in each region, meaning Australia and New Zealand will be among the first to play. Rockstar also clarified physical edition details, announced free digital cover art and a Leonida map, and revealed a stunning new screenshot of downtown Vice City.",
   "txt": "Follow on Google Discover Rockstar Games has confirmed that GTA 6 preloading begins on November 10, 2026, with a download size of up to 212 GB. The game will launch on November 19 at midnight local time in each region, meaning Australia and New Zealand will be among the first to play. Rockstar also clarified physical edition details, announced free digital cover art and a Leonida map, and revealed a stunning new screenshot of downtown Vice City. GTA 6 4.8 34,179+ Reviews Ultimate Edition (Download on This Account, Play on Your Own) $87.35 Buy Now Standard Edition (Download on This Account, Play on Your Own) $69.71 Buy Now summary Rockstar Games has confirmed that GTA 6 preloading begins on November 10, 2026, with a download size of up to 212 GB. The game will launch on November 19 at midnight local time in each region, meaning Australia and New Zealand will be among the first to play. Rockstar also clarified physical edition details, announced free digital cover art and a Leonida map, and revealed a stunning new screenshot of downtown Vice City. Players already planning their in-game progression can also explore options to buy GTA 6 Money once the game becomes available.\nAccording to Rockstar Games' official Newswire announcement, digital preloading for GTA 6 will begin on November 10, 2026, giving players additional time to prepare before launch.\nHowever, the preload schedules differ between PlayStation and Xbox platforms:\nThis means PS5 players can begin downloading the game as soon as November 10 arrives in their respective time zones. Xbox players, meanwhile, will follow one global preload schedule.\nRockstar has also confirmed that physical code-in-box editions for both consoles should become available through retailers starting November 12.\nOne important detail is the game's substantial download requirement. GTA 6 will require up to 212 GB of storage space, depending on the device. Players should check their available storage before the preload date to avoid potential installation problems.\nRockstar has also published a dedicated preload FAQ explaining how to download the game, enable automatic preloading, and troubleshoot common installation issues.\nPerhaps the most important announcement concerns GTA 6's regional release schedule.\nRockstar has confirmed that Grand Theft Auto 6 will launch at 12:00 AM local time on November 19, 2026, across all supported regions on PS5 and Xbox Series X/S.\nUnlike a simultaneous worldwide release, the game will unlock separately as each region reaches midnight.\nThis means players in New Zealand and Australia will be among the first to access GTA 6, followed by other regions across Asia, Europe, and eventually North and South America.\nFor players, this regional release strategy means the exact unlock time depends on their location.\nIt is particularly important for those planning launch-day gaming sessions. Checking the official Rockstar regional release schedule will help avoid confusion about when the game becomes playable.\nRockstar has also clarified what players can expect from the physical code-in-box editions.\nUnfortunately, these editions will not include a physical map of Leonida. Instead, players purchasing the physical version will receive a game activation code.\nOn November 19, the official GTA 6 website will provide downloadable versions of:\nPlayers who prefer physical collectibles will also have another option. Rockstar plans to release a double-sided physical poster shortly after launch through the Rockstar Store.\nIt will cost $99 separately or be available as a free gift with any purchase from the Rockstar Store.\nAlongside the preload announcement, Rockstar released another impressive screenshot showcasing downtown Vice City.\nThe image highlights the incredible environmental detail Rockstar is building into its next open-world experience.\nSeveral interesting elements can be spotted throughout the scene:\n· A private waterfront beach featuring umbrellas, cabanas, and a tiki-style structure.\n· Multiple boats and luxury yachts floating along the coastline.\n· Construction sites, advertisements, and nightclub billboards.\nThe screenshot also features advertisements for the 919 nightclub, demonstrating how Rockstar continues to incorporate recognizable locations and fictional brands into its world.\nThese environmental details help make Vice City feel like a living city rather than simply a collection of missions and activities.\nFollowing the announcement, Rockstar also upda",
