   "t": "GTA 6 vs GTA 5: 15 Gameplay Changes to Police, Robberies, Driving and NPCs",
   "u": "https://www.mmoexp.com/News/gta-6-vs-gta-5-15-gameplay-changes-to-police-robberies-driving-and-npcs.html",
   "img": "https://www.mmoexp.com/mmoexp-v250528/images/mmoexp_logo.png",
   "chapeau": "Discover 15 major GTA 6 vs GTA 5 gameplay differences, from smarter police and expanded robberies to realistic driving, weapon limits, reactive NPCs, and Jason and Lucia",
   "txt": "Follow on Google Discover Discover 15 major GTA 6 vs GTA 5 gameplay differences, from smarter police and expanded robberies to realistic driving, weapon limits, reactive NPCs, and Jason and Lucia's new mechanics. GTA 6 4.8 34,177+ Reviews Ultimate Edition (Download on This Account, Play on Your Own) $87.35 Buy Now Standard Edition (Download on This Account, Play on Your Own) $69.71 Buy Now What if everything you learned about escaping cops in GTA 5 stops working in GTA 6? Breaking line of sight may no longer be enough when officers have your clothes, car and description on record. Rockstar's new police system is only one of 15 gameplay changes that could force longtime Los Santos players to rethink familiar habits, from robbing a store to choosing which guns to carry.\nWith the November 19, 2026 launch approaching and digital preloads beginning November 10, the comparisons are getting easier to make. Developer interviews and pre-release demonstrations describe more involved robberies, heavier driving, a partnership between Jason and Lucia, and more reactive pedestrians. Some changes have been shown in action; how consistently they work across the full game is still an open question.\nIn GTA 5, the familiar escape plan is to break the cops' line of sight and wait for the wanted stars to disappear. GTA 6 adds a Heat system that tracks what the police know about a suspect, including their appearance, clothing, vehicle, weapon and whether they were seen with an accomplice. On-screen icons indicate the identifying details still working against you.\nThat makes changing clothes or abandoning a recognizable car part of the escape itself. If witnesses reported Jason and Lucia together, separating may also remove a useful clue. Losing a patrol car around a corner will no longer guarantee that returning to the same neighborhood in the same outfit is wise.\nGTA 5 caps its wanted level at five stars. GTA 6 restores the sixth, while separately introducing police tools that complicate ordinary chases. During a demonstration observed by Edge, a spike strip punctured a motorcycle tire on a dark road. A K9 unit then caught and pinned Jason. Neither tactic has been established as exclusive to six-star pursuits.\nA quick sports car could still be useful, but players may need another exit when tires fail or an officer's dog closes in. The most interesting unanswered question is how the search escalates from one star to six. The footage confirms more tactical possibilities, not their exact deployment thresholds.\nGTA 5 lets you hold up certain stores, but most free-roam robberies follow a short routine: threaten the clerk, collect the cash and leave. Rockstar has shown a broader system for GTA 6, with different businesses to target, safes to investigate and risks that grow the longer you stay inside.\nImagine the clerk has already handed over the register cash, but a safe is still locked in the back. Finding its combination could preserve the contents; using explosives could damage them. Do you stay while the police close in, or escape with what you have? Demonstrated robberies give that choice weight. Rockstar has not established that every accessible building can be robbed.\nCivilians in GTA 5 mostly panic or flee when a robbery begins. GTA 6's witnesses can be more troublesome. A shopper may intervene, a driver may fight back, and cameras or bystanders can pass information to the police. During one observed hold-up, an ordinary customer tried to stop the crime.\nThe difference is especially important for players who usually rush into a store with a weapon drawn. Checking how crowded a location is, noticing cameras and leaving an exit available may reduce the chance of a minor robbery becoming a long pursuit. Firing the first shot can also affect another new system: your Criminal Profile.\nIn GTA 5, improvising a getaway is often easy because traffic offers an endless supply of cars. GTA 6 makes the fallback less reliable. The vehicle you grab might have a tracker, its owner might be armed, or the tank might be close to empty. Rockstar has explicitly suggested leaving a suitable getaway vehicle near a robbery target.\nThe loot itself can complicate the plan. Earning GTA 6 money from stolen goods may involve more than completing the robbery, especially when valuables must be transported and sold. Preview coverage describes stolen goods that must be carried away and taken to criminal contacts before they become cash. A motorcycle may thread through",
