   "t": "GTA 5’s Unsolvable Mystery Broke Fans for Over a Decade, and GTA 6 Should Do It Again",
   "u": "https://www.polygon.com/gta-5-mount-chiliad-mystery-unsolvable-broke-fans/",
   "img": "https://static0.polygonimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/chorus/uploads/chorus_asset/file/8551343/gta5.jpg?w=1200&h=675&fit=crop",
   "chapeau": "Mt. Chiliad is full of secrets",
   "txt": "In Grand Theft Auto 5 , one landmark was visible practically no matter where you were in San Andreas: Mount Chiliad. \"Claimed by the Spanish in 1769, Mount Chiliad is the highest peak in San Andreas, sitting at a height of 2,744 meters,\" reads a sign at the nearby Silent Probe Mountain art installation. \"Taken under Mexican control in 1821, it was then, and remains in American hands since 1847.\"\nIt's more than just a mountain, though. Once the player has achieved 100% story completion, standing atop the mountain at 3 a.m. during cloudy weather reveals a UFO, hovering in the night sky. It's marked with an F.I.B. logo, aka the Federal Investigation Bureau, implying that it was created by the government. However, there's also reason to believe that the mysterious aircraft is a hoax, because it doesn't react to bullets, and raindrops nearby become pixelated.\nThe running theory is that it's a hologram, as opposed to the two other functional UFOs in the game, which are physical objects. They're located high in the sky above both Fort Zancudo and the Silent Probe Mountain respectively, they can both be collided with, and they emit electromagnetic pulses that cause the player's vehicle to shut down if they get too close. There's reason to believe they're both also government-controlled: the former visually looks somewhat similar to a real-life B-2 Spirit stealth bomber and, when viewed using third-party software, has two human pilots inside. The latter also has F.I.B. printed on the side, much like the UFO above Mt. Chiliad.\nPlayers knew there was at least one secret at the top of the mountain, thanks to graffiti on the back of the observation deck that reads \"come back when your story is complete.\" GTA Online revealed that the mountain is also home to a nuclear launch facility. But some players are convinced that Mt. Chiliad holds one final mystery that is still unsolved to this day.\nInside the tramway station near the summit, a mural depicts an abstract interpretation of the mountain itself. At the top is an eye, while the exterior of the mountain has lightning bolts emanating from it. Inside the mountain is a maze of perpendicular connecting lines. Each one connects to one of eight squares. Five of them are small, marked with an X inside. The three larger ones at the bottom of the picture show, from left to right, a UFO, a cracked egg, and a person wearing a jetpack.\nImage: Rockstar Games via Polygon One week after GTA 5 was released, on Sept. 24, 2013, fans created the Chiliad Mystery subreddit . For the last 13 years, users there have been dedicated to uncovering the secrets believed to be held within. The community worked out that the X's correspond to petroglyphs hidden around the mountain, each of which depicts a weather status required for the Mt. Chiliad UFO to appear. There's also a theory that each X also represents the roman numeral for 10, and since there are five of them, it's representative of the 50 collectible spaceship (aka UFO) parts scattered across San Andreas.\nIn the GTA Online mission involving the nuclear facility, the player escapes by using a jetpack. Is that what the jetpack drawing on the mural is referring to? It’s one of the mural’s lingering riddles. It's certainly plausible, if a little underwhelming, because the common belief was that unraveling the mystery would result in a permanent jetpack vehicle, usable in GTA 5 ’s single-player mode, not exclusive to Online . However, some think the jetpack just refers to the UFO above Fort Zancudo, because in GTA: San Andreas , the jetpack is found at the military base.\nThen there's the cracked egg. This has been the biggest source of confusion for the sleuths working on the mystery, and there are a number of theories. It could refer to the Epsilon cult, as they believe the world hatched from an egg. It could also tie in to the fountain by the Maze Bank Tower in Los Santos, as the two bear a close resemblance. Or there's the most common theory, which is that it is simply a hint to the underwater UFO found in Paleto Bay, on the northern coast of San Andreas.\nImage: Rockstar Games via Polygon So with all of that in mind, there's every chance that the mural is simply one giant hint to finding each of the UFOs in GTA 5 . But believing that would also mean believing that the Chiliad mystery is solved, and there's no fun in that, because it would be a seriously disappointing outcome. And for the users on the subreddit, that isn't even a possibility.\nThere a",
