   "txt": "GTA GTA 6 physical map confirmed as Rockstar reveals new preload date and launch time by Michael Gwilliam Published: Nov 03, 2026, 15:45 Save for later Save for later Rockstar Games Add as a preferred source on Google Follow on Google News Rockstar Games has revealed new details about GTA 6’s upcoming release, confirming that a physical map will be available while also announcing an earlier preload date and launch details.\nWith Grand Theft Auto 6 finally set to launch on November 19, 2026, the countdown to Vice City is officially entering its final stretch.\nOn November 3, Rockstar published a new announcement detailing how players can prepare for launch, including a major change to when downloads will become available.\nThe company also revealed that GTA 6 will require up to 212GB of available storage, depending on the console.\nThat’s slightly more than the 210GB download size previously reported , meaning players may want to start clearing some space now.\nRockstar has officially moved GTA 6’s preload date from November 12 to November 10 , giving players nine days to download the game before its release.\nHowever, the exact time depends on which console you’re using.\nAccording to Rockstar’s updated support page , PlayStation 5 players can begin downloading at midnight local time on November 10.\nXbox Series X|S owners, meanwhile, can start preloading globally at 12 AM GMT on November 10, which works out to 7 PM ET on November 9 in North America.\nRockstar has also confirmed that a map of Leonida will be available as a free download. A physical version will also be available shortly after launch from the Rockstar store for $0.99 or as a free gift included with any purchase.\nFans had been expecting GTA 6’s boxed release to feature a physical map, giving collectors something tangible despite the controversial decision to ship the game without a disc.\nFans have been particularly interested in the physical map after Rockstar accidentally revealed new locations through its $400 Collector’s Edition in September.\nGTA 6 file size revealed and players may want to start clearing storage space\nGTA 6 forces you to take your time with the main story instead of speedrunning it\nAs for when players can actually explore Leonida, GTA 6 launches on November 19, with regional store listings indicating a midnight rollout.\nThis means North American players will be among the last to get access, with New Zealand unlocking the game roughly 18 hours earlier.\nHowever, those desperate to get started might be able to bypass that wait using the popular New Zealand trick, which involves changing console regions or purchasing the game through a New Zealand account.\nWe’ve put together a complete guide explaining how to play GTA 6 early on Xbox and PS5 .\nAfter more than a decade of waiting, GTA 6 is now just over two weeks away.",
