   "txt": "Your login session has expired. Please logout and login again. × Gaming Tech Home Game Release Calendar Gaming PC Builder Will this game run on my PC? Console Comparison Tool More Gaming News PlayStation reportedly bans user for sharing GTA 6 leaked gameplay in PS App PlayStation reportedly bans user for sharing GTA 6 leaked gameplay in PS App By Mudassir Kamran Modified Nov 03, 2026 18:08 IST PlayStation reportedly bans user for sharing GTA 6 leaked gameplay in PS App (Image via Rockstar Games || Sony) PlayStation has reportedly banned a user for sharing leaked GTA 6 gameplay through the PlayStation App, raising concerns among fans ahead of the game's highly anticipated release . The claim surfaced on Reddit, where a user alleged that their friend lost access to their PlayStation Network account shortly after sending the footage to another player.\nAccording to the post, appealing the ban could take up to three months. However, Sony has yet to confirm the incident.\nPlayStation has reportedly banned a user after they shared leaked GTA 6 gameplay through the PlayStation App. The allegation surfaced on Reddit, where user Silver-Succotash-612 claimed that a friend lost access to their PlayStation Network (PSN) account after attempting to send a leaked gameplay clip to another person.\nAccording to the post, the account was banned immediately, and the player was told that the appeal process could take up to three months.\nThe incident has raised questions about how Sony handles leaked content shared through its messaging service. Rockstar Games and its parent company Take-Two Interactive have already taken action against GTA 6 leaks circulating online. However, Sony has not publicly confirmed this specific account suspension.\nThe claim remains unverified, as the Reddit post does not provide independent evidence of the ban or the reported appeal timeline. It is also unclear whether the account received a permanent ban or another form of restriction.\nStill, the allegation serves as a warning for players who share unauthorised gameplay footage through PlayStation services. Users should remain cautious when sharing leaked material, as it could potentially violate platform rules and lead to account restrictions.",
