   "chapeau": "Walmart is trying to get you to buy a disc-less box.",
   "txt": "I just found out that preordering a physical copy of GTA 6 doesn't come with a game disc. You probably knew this already, but you just get a case with a digital voucher slip, meaning you will still need to clear a monstrous 210GB of SSD storage and wait out a massive download queue before stepping foot in Leonida.\nI ditched my console a few years ago ( GTA 6 might persuade me to jump back in), so I'm not exactly the most clued-up gamer, but that feels a little silly to me. What is convincing shoppers to buy a plastic case without an actual disc?\nSpotted by the deal-tracking account Nintendeals, Walmart apparently posted a product listing promising a complimentary \"surprise and delight bag\" bundled with every GTA 6 preorder ($79.99 at Walmart) .\nI guess getting free swag with an $80 purchase that virtually never sees day-one discounts is a harmless win.\nWalmart has history here. It offered promotional snack kits featuring Pringles and Coca-Cola bundled with last year's Nintendo Switch 2 preorders. Getting a novelty can of chips and promotional stickers is not really a compelling reason to buy a plastic case with a paper code inside, but maybe I am simply an old man yelling at a cloud.\nIf you actually want physical collector memorabilia, Rockstar is selling a separate $400 Collector's Box . The 11-piece crate packs custom Oakley sunglasses, a New Era cap, and a physical map of Leonida. But the actual game is sold separately, if you can believe it.\nJoseph Green is the Global Shopping Editor for Mashable. He covers VPNs, headphones, fitness gear, dating sites, streaming, and shopping events like Black Friday and Prime Day.\nJoseph is also Executive Editor of Mashable's sister site, AskMen.",
