   "txt": "Your login session has expired. Please logout and login again. × GTA Home GTA 6 Leaks GTA 6 GTA Online GTA 5 Cheats GTA 5 Cheat Codes Xbox One GTA San Andreas GTA Vice City GTA 5 Phone Cheats GTA V Cheats PS4 GTA 5 Cheats PS3 GTA San Andreas Car Cheats LS Tags GTA Online GTA 3 cheats GTA 4 cheat codes GTA 6 price More GTA All GTA 6 leaks so far All GTA 6 leaks so far By Mohammad Sadiq Modified Nov 02, 2026 13:38 GMT Share \" data-lazy=\"//staticg.sportskeeda.com/comments/ic-comment-v2.png?w=48\" alt=\"comment\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" loading=\"lazy\"/> 0 Discuss Share \" data-lazy=\"//staticg.sportskeeda.com/comments/ic-comment-v2.png?w=48\" alt=\"comment\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" loading=\"lazy\"/> 0 Discuss 0 Discuss What's your opinion? All GTA 6 leaks so far Discuss Now GTA 6 has had several leaks (Image via Rockstar Games) GTA 6 is right around the corner, and while the wait is certainly almost over, what a ride it has been. The game’s long waiting period was marred by leaks over the years, with everything coming to a climax with the infamous Cyberleek situation. The leaks drip-fed us information about the game, its characters, Vice City itself, and more.\nIf you’re eagerly waiting for GTA 6 to release and want a trip down memory lane about all the leaks, we have you covered. In this article, we’ll go over all the GTA 6 leaks that we’ve seen so far. Naturally, there may be some spoilers, so if you wish to walk into the game completely blind, you’ve been warned.\nThe first big GTA 6 leak came at the hands of a GTAForums user named Teapotuberhacker on September 18, 2022. The user leaked files showcasing an early build of the game , giving us our first look at the dual protagonists, Lucia and Jason. The leak also gave us glimpses of the new in-development Vice City , as well.\nThe next big leak came only a few months later, on December 2, 2023, mere days before the first trailer of the game. The leak was made by a TikToker named azzarossi, who was rumored to be the son of a Rockstar North employee . The leak gave us a glimpse of Vice City's skyscrapers and residential areas, as well as a busy highway.\nWith Rockstar's marketing going all in to build up the big Trailer 1 release on December 4, 2023, people were eagerly waiting to get their first official glimpse at the game. Well, some people got that glimpse early thanks to a leak of the entire trailer ahead of the official release. The leaked trailer, rumoured to have been released by a YouTube employee , forced Rockstar's hand and led to the official trailer being released early.\nFast forward to January 1, 2025, and we got a new leak on Reddit. User JustLovett0 shared an image he claimed was from \"mid 2021.\" Furthermore, the user shared a Google Drive link that contained an image of Lucia on a monitor . Next to the monitor was a PS5 development kit , and an Xbox development kit was seen in another video. The office scenery also visually aligned with Rockstar San Diego's, adding credence to the leaks.\nA week later, another Reddit user, Pebblestar_, shared in-game information he claimed was legitimate. According to the user, GTA 6 would feature crash physics resembling real-life crashes , multiple weapon wheels for weapons and attachments, high levels of gore , and allow players to enter 40% of the buildings on the map.\nOn September 8, 2025, dataminer Tez2 revealed that Take-Two Interactive had registered domains for in-game websites . The websites — what-up.app, rydeme.app, buckme.app, leonidagov.org, brianandbradley.com, and more — appeared to be websites you could visit in GTA 6. However, the very next day, Tez2 reported that all of the discovered domains had been removed from Take-Two’s nameservers.\nLater, on November 30, 2025, a demo reel from former Rockstar Toronto character animator Benjamin Chue leaked on Vimeo. The demo reel showed off the game's animations, showing the player character using a bike. The demo reel was later taken down.\nWhile all the leaks up to that point had given us a peek under the lid, a leaker named Cyberleek blew off the lid entirely in August 2026. The leaker leaked several clips from the game, including 25 minutes of GTA 6 gameplay footage later in October.\nThe videos showed them driving around the game's map, interacting with its mechanics. They even threatened to release an entire build of the game online ahead of the game's official release.\nAs far as the contents of the leak are concerned, the gameplay footage gave us a glimpse at the following:",
